@startuml
title SD1 : Notification requested and delivered

actor Recipient
participant "Product Order Delivery and Orchestration Management" as PODOM
participant "//Communication Interaction Management//" as CIM
participant "Party Management" as PM
participant "Party Privacy Management" as PPM
participant "Party Interaction Management" as PIM
participant "Channel Transport" as CT

PODOM -> CIM : 1 **TMF681 Communication Management** POST /communicationMessage\n(messageType="SMS", receiver[].party.id="Alice",\ncontent="Your order 4471 to add Static IP ... confirmed",\npriority="normal", characteristic[messageClass="transactional"])
activate CIM
CIM --> PODOM : 2 **TMF681** 201 Created\n(id, state="initial")
note right of CIM
  The request is accepted independently of whether
  delivery is currently possible (P5, H1).
end note

CIM -> PM : 3 **TMF632 Party Management** GET /individual/Alice\n(fields=contactMedium)
activate PM
PM --> CIM : 4 **TMF632** 200 OK\n(contactMedium[{mediumType="sms", preferred=true, validFor},\n{mediumType="email", preferred=false}])
deactivate PM

CIM -> PPM : 5 **TMF644 Privacy Management** GET the privacy profile for Alice\n(resource level — see Table 12)
activate PPM
PPM --> CIM : 6 **TMF644** 200 OK\n(marketing permitted; no restriction on\n"transactional", "statutory" or "regulatory")
deactivate PPM
note right of PPM
  The profile is read at dispatch rather than held by the
  delivery capability, which is why X6 leaves mastering of
  the profile with Party Privacy Management. Enforcement is what
  moves, not ownership of the consent record.
end note

CIM -> CIM : 7 consent permits "transactional" for this class;\nwithin send window; not a duplicate;\nnothing else in flight for Alice
CIM -> CIM : 8 render for SMS, 160 characters, en-IE;\nselect the preferred medium and a route
CIM -> CT : 9 dispatch on the SMS transport\n(to the mobile number resolved at 4)
activate CT
CT --> Recipient : 10 "Your order 4471 to add Static IP to your\nfibre broadband is confirmed.\nActivation by 12 Sep."
Recipient --> CT : 11 delivery receipt from the handset\n(delivered, timestamp)
CT --> CIM : 12 **transport receipt** delivered, timestamp,\naddress used
deactivate CT
CIM -> CIM : 13 normalise to TMF681 state\n"inProgress" -> "completed"
CIM -> PIM : 14 **TMF683 Party Interaction Management** POST /partyInteraction\n(direction="outbound", status="completed",\nchannel[{name="sms"}], interactionDate,\nrelatedParty[{id="Alice"}])
activate PIM
PIM --> CIM : 15 **TMF683** 201 Created (id)
deactivate PIM
deactivate CIM
note over CIM
  Delivery state is available by query. TMF681 v4.0.0
  defines /hub with no event schemas, so there is no
  event to subscribe to. Recorded in §5.2.
end note

@enduml
